package CanvasNet {
    part def SpecParser {
        doc /* The internal SpecParser (a sealed partial class with static Parse entry points over text or UTF-8 bytes), the immutable tree types (SpecNode, SpecNodeKind, NodePosition, SpecTree), and the SpecMetadata record: a single-pass Utf8JsonReader-based reader with an explicit frame stack that builds the SpecNode tree with lazily computed RFC 6901 pointers and one-based UTF-16 line and column positions for every value and property key, decodes strictly (invalid UTF-8 in bytes and an unpaired surrogate in text are a located VegaLiteSpecException, never U+FFFD), enforces MaxSourceLength (InvalidDataException), MaxJsonDepth, and MaxStringLength (VegaLiteSpecException), applies the duplicate-key policy (last value wins at the position of the first, one vl-duplicate-key warning), and validates the shape of the known properties of views, titles, padding, autosize, mark definitions, channel definitions, data formats (a single-character delimiter, the parse property and its entries, a sequence field name), scales, and axes with rule tables and generous sets of known property names taken from the Vega-Lite 6 JSON schema (a wrong type or value is a VegaLiteSpecException with the pointer of the value; an unknown key is a vl-unknown-property warning); it rejects a schema naming plain Vega, never walks inline data rows, and visits nested views with an explicit work stack. Phase 5 adds, in the partial file SpecParser.Transforms.cs and the SpecExpressions type, the compilation (with the ExpressionParser unit) of every expression text the renderer evaluates (the expression of a calculate transform, a text filter, and the expr references of a mark property or channel value of the drawn view), whose syntax, length, and depth errors and references to an undeclared parameter are a VegaLiteSpecException located at the expression string with the expression offset in the message; the validation of the variable parameters of every view (a repeated or reserved name, a value or expr of the wrong form, and a dependency cycle located at the expression of the lowest declared parameter on the cycle) with the ParameterGraph that orders the parameters dependencies first; and the shape validation of the supported transforms (calculate, filter and its predicates, fold, flatten, sample, pivot, and lookup) of every view. Phase 6 adds the partial file SpecParser.Aggregates.cs, which validates the shape of the aggregate, joinaggregate, window, bin, stack, and impute transforms (operation names, required fields, parameters such as ntile and nth_value, frames, bin parameters, sort fields, and key sequences) and of the aggregate, bin, stack, sort, and order properties of the channel definitions with located errors, and offers the sort-form helpers (IsSupportedSort, the sort shorthand, and the channel a sort refers to) to the other units. A sort array item that is an object or an array (other than a date-time object on a temporal field) is a located error, an array that mixes kinds of values is the warning vl-encoding-sort-mixed-types, and an unknown key of a sort object is a vl-unknown-property warning. Phase 7 adds, in SpecParser.Validation.cs, the validation of the structured options of a scale: the domainMid, domainMin, domainMax, rangeMin, and rangeMax numbers, an interpolate (one of the eight color-space names or an object with that type and a numeric gamma), a scheme (a name or an object with a string name, a positive whole count, and an extent of two numbers), and the bins, with a located error at the offending value and a vl-unknown-property warning for an unknown key of a scheme or interpolate object. SpecMetadata reads the schema URL and major version, the title text, the marks, the data references, and the parameter names from a tree. The condition of a channel definition is validated (an object or an array of objects with a test or a param, located errors) and the test of a condition on a drawn channel is compiled once, a predicate object as the expression that PredicateSource writes for it;         ChannelDefinitions finds the field definition of a conditional channel. Phase 8 adds the partial file SpecParser.Time.cs: the validation of a timeUnit wherever it is written (a name of the documented time units with the utc and binned prefixes, or an object with unit or maxbins, step, utc, and binned; an unknown member is a vl-unknown-property warning), of the datetime objects of a scale domain, domainMin and domainMax, the values of an axis and a legend, the values of a predicate, a sort array of a temporal field, and a datum (each a located error at the wrong member), of the interval of a tickCount or a nice property (one of the eight interval names or an object with an interval and a positive step), of the numeric timeUnitBandPosition and timeUnitBandSize of a mark, of the timeUnit transform (classified as supported), and of the date and utc entries of a parse property (a quoted format is required); PredicateSource writes a time predicate as the expression of Vega-Lite (the datetime of the unit parts of the field against the datetime of the value, the utc functions for a utc unit, the week and dayofyear parts omitted with a warning, a range as two comparisons, oneOf as an index test) and the parser compiles it once under the predicate. Phase 9 validates the properties of the line, area, trail, text, and arc marks (interpolate, tension, point, line, invalid, order, strokeDashOffset, strokeMiterLimit, padAngle, innerRadius, outerRadius, radius, radius2, theta, theta2, text, fontStyle, fontWeight, limit, ellipsis, lineBreak, and lineHeight, and the overlay objects of point and line with the mark rules and a warning for an unknown key), the impute object of a position definition (keyvals bounded by MaxScaleDomainSize, method, value, and frame), and compiles the expression and the conditions of a size value for the line, trail, and text marks. */
                comment sourceRef /* Source: src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/SpecModel/SpecParser.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/SpecModel/SpecParser.Validation.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/SpecModel/SpecParser.Transforms.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/SpecModel/SpecParser.Aggregates.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/SpecModel/SpecParser.Time.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/SpecModel/SpecExpressions.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/SpecModel/SpecNode.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/SpecModel/SpecMetadata.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/SpecModel/ChannelDefinitions.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/SpecModel/PredicateSource.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/SpecModel/NamespaceDoc.cs */
                comment testRef /* Test: test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/SpecModel/SpecParserTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/SpecModel/SpecParserAggregatesTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/SpecModel/SpecParserConditionTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/SpecModel/SpecParserTimeTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/SpecModel/SpecParserMarkTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/SpecModel/SpecParserImputeTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/SpecModel/PredicateSourceTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/SpecModel/PredicateSourceTimeTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/SpecModel/ChannelDefinitionsTests.cs */
        comment designRef /* Design: docs/design/canvas-net-vega-lite/spec-model/spec-parser.md */
        comment verificationRef /* Verification: docs/verification/canvas-net-vega-lite/spec-model/spec-parser.md */
        comment reqRef /* Requirements: docs/reqstream/canvas-net-vega-lite/spec-model/spec-parser.yaml */
    }
}
